<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35791" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pĕtăsus</span></b> , i,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέτασος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a travelling hat</i>
			or <i>cap</i>, with a broad brim (cf.: pileus,
			cucullus). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ps.
				2, 4, 45</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 7, 90</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Am.
				prol. 143</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Arn. 6,
			197</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, something in the shape of a cap,
			placed on a building, <i>a cap</i>, <i>cupola</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 36, 13, 19, §
		92</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
